{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion","id":387388,"title":"Dark Eras: Requiem for Regina Discussion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-31T08:01:21-08:00","id":387388,"title":"Dark Eras: Requiem for Regina Discussion","content":"so no one has yet started a thread for that, and now we have one! :P<br /> <br /> While I'm not that big Vampire fan, but this is one of my fave Eras in the book. The Weihan Cynn are just awesome. I like the fact they don't have some weird blood magic, and instead use the complicate network of contracts and favors. I also wonder what has happened to their old &quot;golden eyes warriors&quot;, and if the other vampires know that the Owls were involved with them in the beginning (and maybe even latter. I haven't found a reference for when/if the strixs stopped being the &quot;mentors&quot; of the group, but I may have missed it. It is a big book after all).<br /> <br /> What that really interest me is the seemingly lacking of Curac like magic- I remember that in Requiem for Rome there was a mention about &quot;barbarians&quot; who use that form of magic. Why does some of the Wood Witches search for a way to revive Veneficia but no one has still met a Curac user? Another point of interest in their writeup is the &quot;Fuil Beannaithe&quot; (or Sacred Blood in Irish according to Google translate). So a rival cult (apparently a pagan one) which come from Ireland? That just touch my Celtic fetish!<br /> <br /> in general, I think that part of the book is written very well, and I really like that chapter. Now I need money to back it up..<br /> <br /> in short, this is awesome. Very awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T08:37:19-08:00","id":387435,"title":"","content":"However much I love more vampire content... it pales somewhat in the light that me running a historical game is fairly low... BUT if I do get to run one - now I know the time period <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T15:52:09-08:00","id":387721,"title":"","content":"When you think about it, the ancient British gods we know of are usually only in recorded history though the Romans' interpretation. Even if there were indigenous blood sorcerers, I can imagine the Roman ones being better remembered, even if the only stories about them were on the continent. &quot;Sacred Blood&quot; sounds a lot like &quot;Blood-Blessed&quot; to me and they look like they combine Catholicism and various pagan beliefs including the Native American ones they can find. In spite of the former Christian heritage, I'm guessing they're more directly related to the Circle of the Crone than the Weihan Cynn. What does &quot;Weihan&quot; mean anyway","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":".  Jack conjugation error. 01-31-2015, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T22:46:54-08:00","id":388024,"title":"","content":"I quite like the Cynn, I think I'd have them absorbed into the Invictus, and be the &quot;black lodge&quot; from Danse Macabre, since their favors system includes trading favors with cosmic forces and saints, for goblin vow like possibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T23:09:36-08:00","id":388049,"title":"","content":"Some thoughts: <br /> <br /> - Aethelgifu is the name of the supposed emperor of the Invictus, from the Invictus sourcebook. Is this the same? In Ancient Mysteries the name of the Night Emperor was forgotten, but in the History of Invictus they mention a lot of people that later we discover they weren't really Invictus, like the Camarilla's Inner Circle, Valea of Byzantium, etc. Which I think is awesome.<br /> <br /> Also, she seems really ancient, even by the time she assumes &quot;praxis&quot;.<br /> <br /> - Felix again! I like the character, but sometimes I wish we knew more of what he is about. I know I can do &quot;whatever I want&quot; with him, but sometimes I feel the books hint of something bigger, a bigger game to him. And not only by curiosity, I wanted to know what that bigger game is, so I could use him better.<br /> <br /> He sometimes seems like a cuckoo. He doesn't only appear somewhere, but he takes someone else's place. That feels weird, but I guess it's a great survival tactic so as people doesn't know his age.<br /> <br /> Also, is he really the same guy from Fall of Camarilla Byzantine part? He feels a lot more like a brute there, and it hints at him being a Khaibit. In his other appearances he seems more like a &quot;suave&quot; kind of guy. And no hint at anything &quot;Khaibit-related.&quot; Perhaps he never really got into Obtenebration. :P<br /> <br /> <br /> - The Cynn are awesome and like others said I love that they're not just a Cruac group, but this network of favors.<br /> <br /> - Sadly, no mention of the Cull that I caught. I was hoping for a bit about it, as Shadows of the UK hint something about the Cull happening each 250 years, and that it happened before. I loved the story about the Faerie Queen, and I probably would tie it to the Cull, instead of the Strix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T23:12:01-08:00","id":388051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Max Deltree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion?p=388049#post388049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Sadly, no mention of the Cull that I caught. I was hoping for a bit about it, as Shadows of the UK hint something about the Cull happening each 250 years, and that it happened before. I loved the story about the Faerie Queen, and I probably would tie it to the Cull, instead of the Strix.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I don't know if it was intended this way, I don't see why the Cull couldn't be the result of the Strix. In fact, if we were utilizing <i>Shadows of the UK </i>it seems rather probably that it is a result of the Owls. Now, <i>why </i>they do it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T17:53:36-08:00","id":389165,"title":"","content":"I kind of want to see some stuff added about the Children's Revolution, they get a mention but aren't fleshed out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T18:32:09-08:00","id":389220,"title":"","content":"Children's Crusade, not Children's Revolution.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I really love the Weihan Cynn. They're exactly what I was looking for but better than I ever imagined.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T05:17:05-08:00","id":389703,"title":"","content":"It was said in the Forums, and confirmed, that Felix was in Requiem for Rome. But i currently don't remember what character was :S","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T06:04:43-08:00","id":389754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion?p=389703#post389703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was said in the Forums, and confirmed, that Felix was in Requiem for Rome. But i currently don't remember what character was :S</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he was Felix, from Fall of the Camarilla. :P<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T06:45:26-08:00","id":389793,"title":"","content":"It is weird, though, as the Felix from FotC is a Mekhet (Khaibit) and the other Felix seems to be Daeva, or at least acts as the stereotypical Serpent, <i>Majesty</i>ing his way around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T08:25:24-08:00","id":389875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion?p=389793#post389793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is weird, though, as the Felix from FotC is a Mekhet (Khaibit) and the other Felix seems to be Daeva, or at least acts as the stereotypical Serpent, <i>Majesty</i>ing his way around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps he secretly is a serial diablerist and all that spirit food got to his personality...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T08:38:57-08:00","id":389890,"title":"","content":"Well, he is (or seems to be) old enough to have needed at some point to feed on other vampires. There's one bad night from that to diablerie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T18:05:48-08:00","id":392087,"title":"","content":"Anyone thought about running a game using <i>Requiem for Regina</i>? I bought the <i>Time Traveler's Guide to Elizabethan England </i>and it's a fun read. I'm trying to see if anything in there inspires a character out of me.<br /> <br /> If not a game, have you guys thought about any concepts suited to the time? There's a lot of interesting threads to pick up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T20:44:18-08:00","id":392225,"title":"","content":"Glad you folks like it! It was quite a big project... more than you might think for just one chapter. It was a lot like doing the research for an entire book and then figuring out what to leave out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion?p=392087#post392087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone thought about running a game using <i>Requiem for Regina</i>? I bought the <i>Time Traveler's Guide to Elizabethan England </i>and it's a fun read. I'm trying to see if anything in there inspires a character out of me.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually the first time I can recall anyone posting that they picked up a non-fiction book recommended in a World of Darkness product. Hurrah!<br /> <br /> There's a section on different types of criminal that's like a big list of character concepts. Perhaps you'd like to play an Upright Man?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T21:01:54-08:00","id":392255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion?p=392225#post392225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glad you folks like it! It was quite a big project... more than you might think for just one chapter. It was a lot like doing the research for an entire book and then figuring out what to leave out.<br /> <br /> This is actually the first time I can recall anyone posting that they picked up a non-fiction book recommended in a World of Darkness product. Hurrah!</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never paid Elizabethan England any mind before, but now I'm fascinated. The Inspiration sections for Dark Eras are pretty great, I intend to watch the movies and see if I can scare up any other fiction (that's good) and set in Elizabethan England as well. I'm research oriented and providing that kind of resource is invaluable to me in describing things and trying to make my game feel properly situated in the setting.<br /> <br /> Quick questions: Ieldra is the Prince's title, right? How do you pronounce her name?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 02-04-2015, 12:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T04:35:10-08:00","id":392504,"title":"","content":"One thing I wanted to mention, and this looks like as good a place as any, is that while a great idea, the way the Dark Eras book is structured it did not push me enough to contribute anything beyond the $5 Requiem PDF tier. I'll probably upgrade my contribution to the full Dark Eras PDF but still, I'd be nice to see historical game lines a la cWoD Dark Ages or Requiem for Rome. Perhaps not as many sourcebooks as the first one but also not as few as just a couple per line.<br /> <br /> Having an entire book, per specific era, per line, just feels more immersive. I'm saying this so that devs and OP don't think the nWoD crowd is stingy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T21:06:02-08:00","id":393410,"title":"","content":"I agree. I think it's the moment, OP begins wth historical gamelines as it did with cWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T15:49:36-08:00","id":394182,"title":"","content":"Question for folks: Do you think the different Clans might use the same names as they did in Rome and in Modern Nights? I'm considering just sticking to nicknames, but I wanted some flavorful ideas on what they might call themselves formally.<br /> <br /> EDIT: For those interested in a map to see different places in London, there's an HD zoomable version of the Agas Map (which was made around the same time as <i>Requiem for Regina</i> takes place, and is one of if not the earliest map of London!) available online <a href=\"http://mapoflondon.uvic.ca/agas.htm\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> Enjoy!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 02-05-2015, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T08:03:48-08:00","id":394841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion?p=394182#post394182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: For those interested in a map to see different places in London, there's an HD zoomable version of the Agas Map (which was made around the same time as <i>Requiem for Regina</i> takes place, and is one of if not the earliest map of London!) available online <a href=\"http://mapoflondon.uvic.ca/agas.htm\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really cool map. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T01:26:52-08:00","id":395967,"title":"","content":"What I am really, really missing is some rules additions on 16th/17th century weapons, in particular firearms &amp; fencing styles.<br /> <br /> Differences to modern weapons are mentioned under Firearms on p.152 in the preview pdf (&quot;Due to their relatively short range, poor accuracy, and tendency to misfire, they are often fired once in combat and then discarded in favor of a melee weapon.&quot;), but there is no rules support.<br /> <br /> I would further like to mention that &quot;To the Stongest&quot; does get weapon charts (p. 50). PLEASE add something like it to the other time periods and Requiem for Regina in particular. This is also the age of D'Artagnan after all and fencing and wheel-/flintlock pistols should receive some love.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1281-aegontargaryen","user":"AegonTargaryen","date":". 02-07-2015, 04:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1281-aegontargaryen","name":"AegonTargaryen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1281_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T18:34:35-08:00","id":397045,"title":"","content":"So is Cruac still practiced by pagan vampires on the continent in this era? It's not like pagan vamps lack those powers in the medical eras in Ancient Mysteries/Bloodlines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T18:49:03-08:00","id":397059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion?p=397045#post397045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So is Cruac still practiced by pagan vampires on the continent in this era? It's not like pagan vamps lack those powers in the medical eras in Ancient Mysteries/Bloodlines.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's blood sorcery elsewhere in the world. Proto-Cruac may even exist in Great Britain, because it'll certainly flourish there in the early nights of the Circle of the Crone. But it's not practiced visibly among vampires in the Ieldra's court.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 02-08-2015, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T13:49:07-08:00","id":397985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion#post387388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Another point of interest in their writeup is the &quot;Fuil Beannaithe&quot; (or Sacred Blood in Irish according to Google translate). So a rival cult (apparently a pagan one) which come from Ireland? That just touch my Celtic fetish!</div> </div> </div> </div>It's difficult to translate into English as it carries aspectual meaning English doesn't mark, but it's a really cool name! It would translate closest to &quot;Blood now blessed&quot; or &quot;Blood in the state of blessedness&quot;. I started trying to think of who they might be &quot;historically&quot;, going the pagan route Crom worshippers might fit, but &quot;beannaithe&quot; is a very Christian adjective so various non-Lancea interpretations of the Kindred in God's plans are possible. To me the name suggests they believe the vampiric state is not a curse and Vitae is spiritually pure. Perhaps ghouling is a holy rite. Anyway lots to muse on! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3326,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","user":"An Fhuiseog","date":". 02-08-2015, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T12:01:02-08:00","id":400616,"title":"","content":"Could someone explain to me why this Era is called Requiem for Regina?<br /> <br /> When I think of Regina I think of the Capital of the Canadian Province <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Saskatchewan. And I can't figure out why we are talking about London nor can I find an answer on Google.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T13:07:14-08:00","id":400745,"title":"","content":"Regina means Queen, and we are talking about Elizabethan London. I think that is it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T13:20:20-08:00","id":400771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion?p=397985#post397985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's difficult to translate into English as it carries aspectual meaning English doesn't mark, but it's a really cool name! It would translate closest to &quot;Blood now blessed&quot; or &quot;Blood in the state of blessedness&quot;. I started trying to think of who they might be &quot;historically&quot;, going the pagan route Crom worshippers might fit, but &quot;beannaithe&quot; is a very Christian adjective so various non-Lancea interpretations of the Kindred in God's plans are possible. To me the name suggests they believe the vampiric state is not a curse and Vitae is spiritually pure. Perhaps ghouling is a holy rite. Anyway lots to muse on! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>sounds really interesting. From what I see, the Elizabethan Era was a time of change in Ireland, as they changed from the Gaelic culture to a monarchic one. The idea of them seeing the state of vampirism as &quot;holy&quot; is really cool, and gives them a feeling of being the &quot;proto Circle&quot; of the British Islands. The fact that the Weihan Cynn see them as rivals means that they both fight for the same &quot;sphere of influence&quot;- either by being connected to the old gods or by trying to make contact with the other denziens of the night. Maybe even both. While they do feel more mystical then the Wood Witches, I wonder what (if any) relationships they have with other supernaturals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T14:49:18-08:00","id":400864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion?p=400771#post400771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> sounds really interesting. From what I see, the Elizabethan Era was a time of change in Ireland, as they changed from the Gaelic culture to a monarchic one. The idea of them seeing the state of vampirism as &quot;holy&quot; is really cool, and gives them a feeling of being the &quot;proto Circle&quot; of the British Islands. The fact that the Weihan Cynn see them as rivals means that they both fight for the same &quot;sphere of influence&quot;- either by being connected to the old gods or by trying to make contact with the other denziens of the night. Maybe even both. While they do feel more mystical then the Wood Witches, I wonder what (if any) relationships they have with other supernaturals.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Blood-Blessed like to proselytise and are said to compete with the Lancea et Sanctum later, so I think their primary sphere of influence is (vampires') hearts and minds. And &quot;returned Blood-Blessed&quot; are mentioned after the Weihan Cynn's expedition to America which I assume means that they were working together, for what that's worth. What's more, \u00c6thelgifu gives them unofficial permission to go back there. I think they end up with a comparable position to that of the Qalandariyyah.<br /> <br /> <br /> I just thought of something. The demographics have changed a bit since <i>Blood and Smoke</i>. For example, Swansea has been mentioned in passing to have had a prince and Ventrue during the 19th century in SotUK and the Ventrue clanbook respectively, as opposed to its Assembly and Ventrue getting lynched shortly after arrival. So maybe in addition to the big five, the Blood-Blessed and Weihan Cynn have survived in parts of the British Isles to present day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 02-10-2015, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T15:50:06-08:00","id":400917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion?p=400745#post400745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regina means Queen, and we are talking about Elizabethan London. I think that is it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T16:53:09-08:00","id":401001,"title":"","content":"I didn't have any problems finding Regina aka The Evil Queen on Google.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&amp;source=univ&amp;sa=X&amp;ei=J6jaVLu2IoemNrfmgoAD&amp;ved=0CB8QsAQ&amp;biw=1420&amp;bih=732&amp;q=Regina+once+upon+a+time\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&amp;source=univ&amp;sa=X&amp;ei=J6jaVLu2IoemNrfmgoAD&amp;ved=0CB8QsAQ&amp;biw=1420&amp;bih=732&amp;q=Regina+once+upon+a+time\" target=\"_blank\"> Google Search </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&amp;source=univ&amp;sa=X&amp;ei=J6jaVLu2IoemNrfmgoAD&amp;ved=0CB8QsAQ&amp;biw=1420&amp;bih=732&amp;q=Regina+once+upon+a+time\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.google.com/search?tbm=isch&amp;source=univ&amp;sa=X&amp;ei=J6jaVLu2IoemNrfmgoAD&amp;ved=0CB8QsAQ&amp;biw=1420&amp;bih=732&amp;q=Regina+once+upon+a+time </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T03:27:43-08:00","id":403140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion?p=388051#post388051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I don't know if it was intended this way, I don't see why the Cull couldn't be the result of the Strix. In fact, if we were utilizing <i>Shadows of the UK </i>it seems rather probably that it is a result of the Owls. Now, <i>why </i>they do it...</div> </div> </div> </div>In Mr. Theleme's Story in Night Stalkers, wasn't there a sequence where he gets lead by Tanner, the one vampire that survived the Cull i think, into a strix meeting place and ambush in a cemetary? Thought it was worth pointing out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T13:47:59-08:00","id":403652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion?p=400745#post400745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regina means Queen, and we are talking about Elizabethan London. I think that is it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks! It never occured to me to look up translation from Old English and other languages from the region!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T15:42:25-08:00","id":405222,"title":"","content":"I'm really excited that the <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/world-of-darkness-dark-eras-prestige-edition/posts/1135264\" target=\"_blank\">next stretch goal</a>, for which the poll is now open, could let us show how changelings fit into this picture.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T00:47:28-08:00","id":405561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion?p=405222#post405222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really excited that the <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/world-of-darkness-dark-eras-prestige-edition/posts/1135264\" target=\"_blank\">next stretch goal</a>, for which the poll is now open, could let us show how changelings fit into this picture.</div> </div> </div> </div>And thanks to the crossover potential of the Weihan Cynn it fits quite nicely into the picture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-14T02:26:40-08:00","id":405609,"title":"","content":"Yes, it would be so awesome ! Reading Requiem for Regina, it feel like knowing wath's going on on the changeling side is the thing to understand the wole picture. To bad for now this choice is second... We still have time to turn the table, I hope we will make it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3883-arabidopsis","name":"Arabidopsis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T23:06:45-08:00","id":407421,"title":"","content":"What kind of foreigners would be the most commonly seen in Elizabethan London? Do you guys have any thoughts on what groups of Kindred might travel there, besides Kindred from other parts of England?<br /> <br /> I'm fiddling around with a Gallow's Post character, who foremost made themselves useful by being a polyglot that speaks &amp; reads a bunch of different languages, and often helps welcome foreigners to the city by translating for them, so I'm trying to figure out what kinds of foreign Kindred might most commonly pass through. Right now my languages are French, Italian, Latin and Greek. What others might you guys propose?<br /> <br /> P.S. I heartily recommend the listed <i>A Time Traveler's Guide to Elizabethan England </i>for anybody that wants to run this setting. It's great for getting a sense of what the place is actually like, what people really do, and is loaded with the kinds of details that can flesh out a character's life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 02-16-2015, 02:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T02:09:11-08:00","id":407514,"title":"","content":"Irish Gaelic, Scottish Gaelic, Welsh, Spanish, Portuguese, Dutch, German. If you want to be exotic, Coptic, Arabic, Hebrew, Farsi/Persian, Basque, Finnish, Norwegian, or Icelandic. If you want to stretch credibility a bit, the individual could have picked up the Secotan, Croatan, Beothuk and/or Powhatan languages traveling with Walter Raleigh and associates like Thomas Harriot. Manteo and Wanchese allegedly spoke and understood enough Spanish already to communicate with Raleigh's entourage when they first arrived.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","user":"Audrey St. John","date":". 02-16-2015, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T10:25:09-08:00","id":412928,"title":"","content":"African languages as well, while not as popular as in Continental cultures, lots of people had black servants or slaves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T11:42:07-08:00","id":412966,"title":"","content":"I just posted an art piece from the chapter that I really like: <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/world-of-darkness-dark-eras-prestige-edition/posts/1141981\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects.../posts/1141981</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T12:45:52-08:00","id":413040,"title":"","content":"Nice Art...Thanks for Sharing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T22:08:31-08:00","id":417197,"title":"","content":"So I'm starting to write up some more characters to go along with the existing types of people, and its got me wondering about the Gallow's Post. What's their organization like? Since they seem professional and neutral, it seems to me like they've have a hierarchy of sorts, but the factions seem to cover broad services. If there is one guy who is top dog of the Gallow's Post in a given domain, what might we call him? <br /> <br /> I'm just pondering this while I consider what characters I feel might be interest for more Kindred of Power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T03:18:58-08:00","id":417397,"title":"","content":"I would go with &quot;Ferryman&quot; (official) or &quot;Smuggler&quot; (illegal goods and beings)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3883-arabidopsis","name":"Arabidopsis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T02:54:15-08:00","id":418550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion?p=412966#post412966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just posted an art piece from the chapter that I really like: <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/world-of-darkness-dark-eras-prestige-edition/posts/1141981\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects.../posts/1141981</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nice one! I have one question, though (well, two, but only one related to the picture): who might be that vampire? I was thinking about Carmilla, but maybe i'm failing there! <br /> <br /> The second question is this: almost all other splat has had two new Eras in the kickstarter goals, and some even three (i'm looking slightly resentfully at you, Changeling) but Vampire hasn't. I'm curious about the why behind the fact, as is one of the perfect splats to see history through. Although i'm complaining (man i'd love to see the Vampire Black Death period) i'm more curious than frustrated, as we already have that monumental work, Requiem for Rome. But still... curious about it. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T03:05:39-08:00","id":418553,"title":"","content":"Why Vampire haven't a second setting ? I would say because it had bad match up, every time Vampire was in a poll it is against Changeling (who won each time). But the extension Vampire got is thanks to changeling, so don't hate them to much ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3883-arabidopsis","name":"Arabidopsis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T03:58:55-08:00","id":418573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arabidopsis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion?p=418553#post418553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why Vampire haven't a second setting ? I would say because it had bad match up, every time Vampire was in a poll it is against Changeling (who won each time). But the extension Vampire got is thanks to changeling, so don't hate them to much ^^</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it kind of funny how the one time Vampire won the poll... it still involed Changelings. Makes you wonder if a Strix has made some deals to spite the Kindred...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T04:20:48-08:00","id":418587,"title":"","content":"And I think most of the polls where pretty &quot;front loaded&quot;. All in all, I'm quite disappointed in the whole vote thing","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T04:40:29-08:00","id":418593,"title":"","content":"Perhaps, if something similar was done in the future, it might be best to release a large multiple-choice poll (maybe up to 5 possible picks?) before the Kickstarter even starts and then simply work down the Stretch Goals from the most popular down to the least popular option. If the Kickstarter would actually end up going through all of them, a few additional options wouldn't be a major issue, I think.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit</b>: That would also give both the developers and interested users on the forum enough time to post cool pitches for their favourite eras, to fish for votes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T04:44:07-08:00","id":418595,"title":"","content":"That will still be as front loaded as this, because some of the options were really phrased terribly, while their image was much better as discussed on the forums... but they failed because they had a much better pitched name next to them (Grimm's Changeling??? That was an instant win when placed to the other ones, simply because the other ones weren't &quot;sold&quot; as well in the name.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T06:35:58-08:00","id":418650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion?p=418550#post418550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice one! I have one question, though (well, two, but only one related to the picture): who might be that vampire? I was thinking about Carmilla, but maybe i'm failing there!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, Carmilla Incarnadine, soon to be Princess of Dublin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion?p=418550#post418550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second question is this: almost all other splat has had two new Eras in the kickstarter goals, and some even three (i'm looking slightly resentfully at you, Changeling) but Vampire hasn't. I'm curious about the why behind the fact, as is one of the perfect splats to see history through. Although i'm complaining (man i'd love to see the Vampire Black Death period) i'm more curious than frustrated, as we already have that monumental work, Requiem for Rome. But still... curious about it. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no particular reason, just which pitches stood out as we were picking poll options. <i>Vampire</i>'s had more historical material in the past, though, with <i>Requiem for Rome</i>, &quot;Slouching Towards Byzantium&quot; in <i>Fall of the Camarilla</i>, <i>Ancient Mysteries</i>, and <i>New Wave Requiem</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T02:49:59-08:00","id":419990,"title":"","content":"Well, i'd have a suggestion about the polls, seeing i'm not the only one dissappointed with them: one solution to the problem of multiples votes coming from only one person could be giving the right to vote only to backers of the kickstarter. Those who would pledge 1$ or more are allowed to vote, only once per stretch goal. Maybe with successive investment one person could vote more times? Anyway, those are my two cents on the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T04:01:27-08:00","id":420036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion?p=419990#post419990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, i'd have a suggestion about the polls, seeing i'm not the only one dissappointed with them: one solution to the problem of multiples votes coming from only one person could be giving the right to vote only to backers of the kickstarter. Those who would pledge 1$ or more are allowed to vote, only once per stretch goal. Maybe with successive investment one person could vote more times? Anyway, those are my two cents on the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question is how would that be done technically? I do not think Kickstarter has an internal poll option (yet). How could OP easily verify the identity of voters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T05:30:26-08:00","id":420070,"title":"","content":"Maybe it could be verified here in the forums? we could write in a post our names and the option we vote for. Much more clear in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T18:07:11-08:00","id":422375,"title":"","content":"Another <i>Regina </i>question, for clarification on Felix impersonating Lord Walsingham... How is that possible, exactly? Does he just come up with excuses for missing meetings during the day or what? <br /> <br /> Rather, how do you guys think Felix is pulling that charade off? Moreover, is he just assuming his identity or does he have some means of looking like him, too?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T18:17:39-08:00","id":422378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion?p=422375#post422375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another <i>Regina </i>question, for clarification on Felix impersonating Lord Walsingham... How is that possible, exactly? Does he just come up with excuses for missing meetings during the day or what?<br /> <br /> Rather, how do you guys think Felix is pulling that charade off? Moreover, is he just assuming his identity or does he have some means of looking like him, too?</div> </div> </div> </div>He is using Dominate to <b>assume direct control.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T18:19:08-08:00","id":422379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion?p=422378#post422378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He is using Dominate to <b>assume direct control.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>The funeral at the end of his character blurb presents an interesting conundrum in that case. It also makes his apparent survival of the assassination attempt in the fiction also seem a bit odd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T16:26:04-08:00","id":424640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Audrey St. John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion?p=407514#post407514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Irish Gaelic, Scottish Gaelic, Welsh, Spanish, Portuguese, Dutch, German. If you want to be exotic, Coptic, Arabic, Hebrew, Farsi/Persian, Basque, Finnish, Norwegian, or Icelandic. If you want to stretch credibility a bit, the individual could have picked up the Secotan, Croatan, Beothuk and/or Powhatan languages traveling with Walter Raleigh and associates like Thomas Harriot. Manteo and Wanchese allegedly spoke and understood enough Spanish already to communicate with Raleigh's entourage when they first arrived.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, Historian/game designer here (I have a Call of Cthulhu project involving this time period). You have forgotten the Italians... some very interesting ones are in London at the time: Giordano Bruno, Aemilia Lanyer (half-Italian/Jewish), and my own Castiglione ancestors among others. There are also Poles and Russians associated with the Moscovy Company, Turks (presumably) with the Levant Company, and Portuguese Jews, and, of course, Romani.<br /> <br /> I've studied Kit Marlowe, John Dee, and the Walsinghams at length, if anyone is interested in them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1966-jeffjerwin","name":"Jeffjerwin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T16:48:48-08:00","id":424661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeffjerwin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion?p=424640#post424640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey, Historian/game designer here (I have a Call of Cthulhu project involving this time period). You have forgotten the Italians... some very interesting ones are in London at the time: Giordano Bruno, Aemilia Lanyer (half-Italian/Jewish), and my own Castiglione ancestors among others. There are also Poles and Russians associated with the Moscovy Company, Turks (presumably) with the Levant Company, and Portuguese Jews, and, of course, Romani.<br /> <br /> I've studied Kit Marlowe, John Dee, and the Walsinghams at length, if anyone is interested in them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am intensely interested in all of these things. Do you have anything to share based on what's in Requiem for Regina? Or any suggestions on what to add to the setting based upon your additional knowledge?<br /> <br /> What's that CoC project called? that's another game I like.<br /> <br /> Something I noticed: The Lambton Worm is cited as a mythicalish example of one of the things the Weihan Cynn could have a contract with. Incidentally, the Lambton Worm is apparently mentioned in the Gangrel Clanbook...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T17:05:37-08:00","id":424682,"title":"","content":"Well, you may want to read up on cunning men and Simon Forman for more ideas. Dee's library was fairly famous and is a day's journey from the city. There's an interesting book called &quot;Under the Molehill&quot; (a companion to Giordano Bruno and the Embassy Affair) both by John Bossy. Kendall's &quot;Christopher Marlowe and Richard Baines&quot; is very very interesting, as is The Reckoning by Charles Nicholl. I'd look into the mysterious death of Lord Strange (possibly an early patron of Shakespeare) at around the same time...<br /> <br /> To, Elizabethan London is a great Mage setting as well, given the &quot;School of Night&quot; and the alchemical symbolism scattered everywhere in poetry and theatre at the time (the same argument could be made for an awesome Promethean game, actually).<br /> <br /> The use of alchemy by women (as by the Countess of Cumberland and her daughter), and the queer-ness of so much spy craft at the time, along with theatre, is also thematically apposite to any number of interesting games. There was a great deal of skullduggery because of the precarious situation of Elizabeth viz a viz Hapsburg-dominated Europe.<br /> <br /> Then one could take a Spenserian rote re the Changelings and make the Queen the fetch of Gloriana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1966-jeffjerwin","name":"Jeffjerwin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T19:12:15-08:00","id":427232,"title":"","content":"What language is &quot;Weihan Cynn&quot; and what does it mean? Does it actually mean Wood Witches?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T19:36:51-08:00","id":427247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion?p=427232#post427232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What language is &quot;Weihan Cynn&quot; and what does it mean? Does it actually mean Wood Witches?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's quasi-Old English/Anglo-Saxon (actually Old German + AS). It means &quot;sacred folk&quot;. Grimm linked wicca, vicce, 'enchantment' and 'magic' to weihan, an old Gothic root.<br /> See here: <a href=\"http://theheadlesshashasheen.tumblr.com/post/88225450102/online-etymology-dictionary\" target=\"_blank\">http://theheadlesshashasheen.tumblr....ogy-dictionary</a><br /> <br /> Err... just as in V:tR with Lancea Sanctum, the linguistics are a bit off. The real AS words would be Wicce Cynn. I don't suppose it's too late to fix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1966-jeffjerwin","name":"Jeffjerwin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T16:24:35-08:00","id":429413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeffjerwin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion?p=427247#post427247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's quasi-Old English/Anglo-Saxon (actually Old German + AS). It means &quot;sacred folk&quot;. Grimm linked wicca, vicce, 'enchantment' and 'magic' to weihan, an old Gothic root.<br /> See here: <a href=\"http://theheadlesshashasheen.tumblr.com/post/88225450102/online-etymology-dictionary\" target=\"_blank\">http://theheadlesshashasheen.tumblr....ogy-dictionary</a><br /> <br /> Err... just as in V:tR with Lancea Sanctum, the linguistics are a bit off. The real AS words would be Wicce Cynn. I don't suppose it's too late to fix.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, that is a bit too close to Wicca, so it brings the mind immediately to more modern witchcraft, as well as the Circle of the Crone, so that might be intentional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T22:50:49-08:00","id":429881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion?p=429413#post429413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On the other hand, that is a bit too close to Wicca, so it brings the mind immediately to more modern witchcraft, as well as the Circle of the Crone, so that might be intentional.</div> </div> </div> </div>Modern Wicca took the word from A-S/OE. Of course one could have used Halig and had the same meaning, or very close.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1966-jeffjerwin","name":"Jeffjerwin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T22:58:50-08:00","id":429884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeffjerwin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion?p=429881#post429881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Modern Wicca took the word from A-S/OE. Of course one could have used Halig and had the same meaning, or very close.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he's aware, he's speaking to what Wicca means in the popular context. The problem isn't the A-S/OE component, but that people would make the association between the Weihan Cynn and the Circle of the Crone more close than it should be/is.<br /> <br /> Question: So I've been doing some casual expanded NPC writing for the setting. Would anybody be interested in seeing some additional odds and ends characters to throw into <i>Requiem for Regina</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T05:01:09-08:00","id":430028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion?p=429884#post429884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think he's aware, he's speaking to what Wicca means in the popular context. The problem isn't the A-S/OE component, but that people would make the association between the Weihan Cynn and the Circle of the Crone more close than it should be/is.<br /> <br /> Question: So I've been doing some casual expanded NPC writing for the setting. Would anybody be interested in seeing some additional odds and ends characters to throw into <i>Requiem for Regina</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's exactly what I meant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T19:22:03-07:00","id":436547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion?p=430028#post430028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that's exactly what I meant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I suspect, that the mistake actually comes from an ambiguously worded passage in Grimm, rather than a deliberate choice. In any case, since the modern root is written weihs, not weihan, the source is certainly either Grimm or a commentary on their work. The word would never have been used for &quot;sacred&quot; or such in Dark Age England, since Gothic was a continental language at some remove from Anglo-Saxon. I actually was quite surprised that the Covenant had no Cruac-like powers given its name, since I recognized the word. I will probably call them A<span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u00fe Cyn (Oath-Kind) in my version to keep the (personal) </span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">cognitive</span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> dissonance at bay...</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1966-jeffjerwin","name":"Jeffjerwin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T19:36:20-07:00","id":436556,"title":"","content":"Probably a stupid question, but is it 'Reg-ee-na' or 'Reg-eye-na?'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T22:21:00-07:00","id":436734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion?p=436556#post436556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably a stupid question, but is it 'Reg-ee-na' or 'Reg-eye-na?'</div> </div> </div> </div>In English, the former. The latter in the original Latin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T11:36:43-07:00","id":440205,"title":"","content":"What do you guys think might be significant neighboring Domains to Elizabethan London? I mean both ones in the greater UK as well as London's actual neighbors/nearby cities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T16:14:15-07:00","id":440551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion?p=440205#post440205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you guys think might be significant neighboring Domains to Elizabethan London? I mean both ones in the greater UK as well as London's actual neighbors/nearby cities.</div> </div> </div> </div>There would probably be domains around Birmingham, Nottingham, Yorkshire, Oxford, Manchester and Liverpool. They would be very focused though as London was an order of magnitude larger than the others. I'd imagine most other domains would be quite rural. In the broader UK perhaps Norwegian kindred from the 10th century invasions would still be around with strongholds along the Scottish isles, as well as old Welsh kindred deep in lairs among the Welsh valleys. (Oxford would be an interesting meeting point for them and English kindred).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T21:47:23-07:00","id":445348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion?p=440551#post440551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There would probably be domains around Birmingham, Nottingham, Yorkshire, Oxford, Manchester and Liverpool. They would be very focused though as London was an order of magnitude larger than the others. I'd imagine most other domains would be quite rural. In the broader UK perhaps Norwegian kindred from the 10th century invasions would still be around with strongholds along the Scottish isles, as well as old Welsh kindred deep in lairs among the Welsh valleys. (Oxford would be an interesting meeting point for them and English kindred).</div> </div> </div> </div>Going by wikipedia (<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_towns_and_cities_in_England_by_historical_population\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of...cal_population</a>) the top ten towns in England (in 1523) by population were London, followed by Norwich, Bristol, Newcastle, Coventry, Exeter, Salisbury, Ipswich, King's Lynn, and Canterbury. Canterbury, Ipswich, and Norwich are no more than a few days' ride, but the others are more distant. By 1662 York has risen in the ranks along with Great Yarmouth, Oxford, and Cambridge, and Canterbury and Salisbury have receded (Lynn has totally dropped off the list). Birmingham, Liverpool, and Manchester are all products of the Industrial Revolution which has yet to occur. Nottingham is a smaller town but has some interesting caves. While population is not necessarily connected to Kindred domains I'd venture that since most of these towns were medieval trading centers they would have had more vampires and more powerful ones. You may want to consider Anglo-Saxon and Roman sites that have fallen into obscurity for elders, however, as well as fortresses, so perhaps Rochester, Pevensey, Dover, the Chiltern hills and the Essex forests, Winchester, Silchester, and Doncaster as interesting places with considerable history. There are also the Catuvellauni settlements, such as Verulamium (St Albans) and the Iceni of Norfolk - the folk of Boudicca - for old and dangerous powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1966-jeffjerwin","name":"Jeffjerwin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T11:06:43-07:00","id":446201,"title":"","content":"Ah, my knowledge of early modern England is hilarious off then! What is/was in the Essex forests actually, sounds interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T07:13:43-07:00","id":450412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion?p=446201#post446201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, my knowledge of early modern England is hilarious off then! What is/was in the Essex forests actually, sounds interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you've got Epping (then known as Waltham) forest, a woodland to the northeast of London in Essex. It contains a royal hunting lodge that still stands. Further away you have Hatfield forest, Writtle, and Kingswood. All are remnants of a much large forest that once covered Essex. These are real forests, not just hunting preserves. See this site: <a href=\"http://info.sjc.ox.ac.uk/forests/index.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://info.sjc.ox.ac.uk/forests/index.html</a> (&quot;Forests and Chases of England and Wales&quot;). It has maps, info on forest law, and images.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1966-jeffjerwin","name":"Jeffjerwin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T22:22:55-07:00","id":458673,"title":"","content":"Anyone thought of any cool epithets for the Gallow's Post? I've been writing expanded material for them for my own games, focusing on the culture they foster. Really, they feel to me like a perfect criminal organization of the Damned, and one of the things I'm imagining as being unique to them is how they might mingle with the mortal underworld as well. I'm looking for other descriptors they might use for themselves, and Postmen felt a little silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T12:53:07-07:00","id":460335,"title":"","content":"Cool bit of material I stumbled on for adding other interesting parties to Elizabethan England as a setting<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crime in Early Modern England 1550-1750 By James A Sharpe</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Thus, in 1585, following what appears to be an unusually active drive against crime by the London authorities, a remarkable report was sent to Lord Burghley. This not only listed a number of notorious thieves and fourty five &quot;harbouringe howses&quot; for criminals, but also described a school of pickpockets suggestive of the presence of an Elizabethan Fagin.<br /> <br /> 'One Wotton, a gentilman borne,' the report ran, had &quot;procured all the cutpurses about this cittie to repair to his said howse. There was a schole howse sett upp to learne younge boyes to cutt purses.' Among the teaching aids at this unusual academy was a purse containing counters and money which was hung with bells. The youngsters were taught to take money out of the purses without sounding the bells, 'and he that could take a peece of sylver out of the purse without the noyse of any of the bells, he was adjudged a judiciall Nypper.' Such accounts do lend substance to literary evidence of the existence of an 'Elizabethan underworld.'</div> </div> </div> </div>While the story itself may not be true (It's apparently from real Tudor court documents that were compiled in 1924, but who knows if the original documents are actually true.), the idea is absolute gold. Especially in light of other famous stories of pickpocket schools, like the <a href=\"http://pickpocket.blog.ca/2010/08/19/school-of-seven-bells-9205095/\" target=\"_blank\">School of the Seven Bells</a>.<br /> <br /> Nevermind that the gentleman Wotton sounds like a cool character addition to any game set in Elizabethan England, combining the idea of his school with a more mythical version of the School of the Seven Bells sounds almost worthy of its own Mystery Cult Initiation writeup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T08:08:50-07:00","id":472772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/387388-dark-eras-requiem-for-regina-discussion?p=458673#post458673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone thought of any cool epithets for the Gallow's Post? I've been writing expanded material for them for my own games, focusing on the culture they foster. Really, they feel to me like a perfect criminal organization of the Damned, and one of the things I'm imagining as being unique to them is how they might mingle with the mortal underworld as well. I'm looking for other descriptors they might use for themselves, and Postmen felt a little silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Tyburn&quot; &quot;Ah; Tyburn is here&quot; or &quot;Tyburn sends her regards&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1966-jeffjerwin","name":"Jeffjerwin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T09:32:45-08:00","id":823437,"title":"","content":"I've recently started a PbP game of Requiem for Regina, and I'm really proud of how it's turning out to be. Researching a bit among other Chronicles of Fucking Darkness books, I've gathered a bit more of material to use in that game. Here's two funny thoughts I had while doing so:<br /> <br /> - Is Ce\u00e7il actually Elisabeta, the Plague Nun? She does actually show up in my game in normal circumstances and active. I'm probably using Ce\u00e7il as her actual Shadow.<br /> <br /> - Also, Greta from Clanbook Gangrel's description seems very similar to the Ieldra. Probably just a coincidence, as I think she is a Mekhet, not Gangrel. But Greta's backstory seems to fit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T10:59:53-08:00","id":823510,"title":"","content":"Totally going to have to re-read that section.<br /> <br /> Secily does sound like Elisabeta, especially with the fondness for young women.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-04-2016, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T20:48:57-08:00","id":823978,"title":"","content":"Worthh looking at: Ken Hite's mini-supplement regarding magic spies in the Elizabethan era. It's GUMSHOE, not CofD, but it deals eith enough occult stuff and spies to be worth a read.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/138064/The-School-of-Night?term=School+of+&amp;cPath=561_22009\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/340/138064.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/138064/The-School-of-Night?term=School+of+&amp;cPath=561_22009\" target=\"_blank\"> The School of Night - Pelgrane Press | GUMSHOE System | Trail of Cthulhu | Esoterrorists | Mutant City Blues | Night's Black Agents | Ken Writes About Stuff | DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/138064/The-School-of-Night?term=School+of+&amp;cPath=561_22009\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/138064/The-School-of-Night?term=School+of+&amp;cPath=561_22009 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The School of Night - The School of Night &ldquo;Black is the badge of Hell; the hue of dungeons and the School of Night.&rdquo; Queen Elizabeth&rsquo;s r </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T10:20:03-08:00","id":833367,"title":"","content":"So, for my game I've compiled every named character I've come across the Requiem for Regina chapter.<br /> <br /> <br /> The ones with Write-up:<br /> <br /> Ieldra \u00c6thelgifu: Mekhet, Queen of the Weyhan Cynn. Very ancient, born around 950 (real daughter of Alfred). A pale bony woman. Appears around the Black Death.<br /> <br /> Clement the Moor: Embraced by the Ieldra herself. Might have been embraced at the beginning of Elizabethan's reign, a bit before at best.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">C\u00e6dmon the Lloegyrwys: Archebishop of the Lancea et Sanctum. Daeva, I would guess. Amber-eyed poet, who came to London after the Lincolnshire rising (around 1536).</span></span><br /> <br /> Richard Bithewaye: Power Broker of the Invictus. Probably Ventrue. Very old and crass. Embraced by <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Bithewaye the Elder (who he killed).</span></span><br /> <br /> Cicely Rowe: Invictus Climber. Probably Daeva or Ventrue. I think she's a neonate, given her write-up. Real person with this name marries the mayor of London, Sir William Rowe.<br /> <br /> Adam Nomen: <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Once Invictus, now of The School of Night.</span></span><br /> <br /> Felix: Felix being Felix, like usual. Mekhet, Khaibit blood. Was embraced around 540, probably a bit before.<br /> <br /> Se\u00e7il: Very probably Elisabeta. If so, then Mekhet of Morbus Bloodline. Active since around 300 a.d. in Rome.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The ones just mentioned: </span></span><br /> <br /> Sir Thomas Gresham: Was a real person, so probably wasn't embraced very long ago. Very strong, so probably Daeva. Merchant, so I would guess Invictus.<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Camilah/Carmilla: Future Prince of Dublin in 18th century. Daeva. Not sure if present in Elizabethan London, but why not?</span></span><br /> <br /> Kismet: Gallow's Post. A <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Daeva neonate hailing from the Ottoman Empire, embraced by Camilah/Carmilla. Future Prince after the Ieldra. As he's a neonate when he climbs to power, he might not be embraced before 1630.</span></span><br /> <br /> Benjamin Cahill: Invictus. <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">He is a relatively young Lord, with his </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Embrace falling just before the death of Christopher Marlowe (1593). Tries to become the Prince after 1666, but fail miserably.</span></span><br /> <br /> Tarquin St. John: <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Sanctified Shadow who also traveled to London with </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">the resurgence of the Gallows Post in 1666. For Tarquin, however, it was a return home, so he was active before the withdraw. Becomes prince/Archbishop after Kismet leaves.</span></span><br /> <br /> Paul Michael Hill: Invictus. <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">A transplant from Ireland, having come to London during the reign of Good Queen </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Bess. Becomes Prince after St. John. Strong connection to Carmilla, I guess.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Charles Emerson: Creator of the Westminster Creed of the Lancea et Sanctum.</span></span><br /> <br /> Sister Fortune: <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Simon Loveney\u2019s sire.</span></span><br /> <br /> Simon Loveney: N<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">eonate freshly Embraced into the Daeva and the Lancea et Sanctum. Causes trouble at one story.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> If anyone has any correction or know of any other character mentioned or detailed in any book who might be active at the time, it would be appreciated. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}